Title: THE GROOMSMEN'S GUIDE
Author: Marcus Webb
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. TUXEDO SHOP - DAY

DAVE KIM, 30s, groom-to-be, holds up two identical navy tuxes. His best man TOM and cousin PETE sit on a velvet bench.
DAVE
Same cut, same color. No one starts a wedding brawl over lapels.
TOM
Last time I wore rental shoes, I lost a toenail and a girlfriend.

INT. STRIP MALL BAR - NIGHT

The guys clink beers. A MAGNETIC GUEST BOOK sits in Dave's backpack.
PETE
Your fiancée said no surprises. This is a surprise with a power cord.
DAVE
It's a guest book that displays photos. Romantic. Technically.

INT. REHEARSAL DINNER - NIGHT

Dave's future mother-in-law DIANE inspects place cards. Dave sweats near the podium.
DIANE
Short speeches. No props. My daughter hates props.
TOM
(to Dave)
Hide the magnetic thing. I'm begging you.

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - DAY

Wedding morning chaos. PETE irons a sash. The MAGNETIC GUEST BOOK accidentally clings to a metal door frame.
PETE
Dave, your romantic technology is stuck to the service entrance.

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - NIGHT

Reception in full swing. Dave taps the mic. The guest book lights up — and projects every rehearsal-dinner toast, including Tom's drunk one.
DAVE
Before I introduce my wife, I'd like to apologize to her mother, science, and this ballroom.

FADE OUT.


THE END
